---
import MarketingSite from '../layouts/MarketingSite.astro';
import LiveQueue from '../components/LiveQueue.astro';
import authorAvatar from '../assets/johnny-domino.png';
import arrowLeftUrl from '../assets/icons/arrow-left.svg?url&no-inline';

const title = 'Workcell';
const description = 'A FIFO queue for the Macs, phones, GPUs, and rigs that coding agents share.';
---

<MarketingSite title={title} description={description}>
  <main id="main-content" class="post-main">
    <article>
      <header class="post-header post-width">
        <a class="back-link" href="https://github.com/jmonster/workcell">
          <img src={arrowLeftUrl} width="16" height="16" alt="" />
          View on GitHub
        </a>

        <h1>{title}</h1>
        <p class="dek">A FIFO queue for the Macs, phones, GPUs, and rigs that coding agents share.</p>

        <div class="byline">
          <a href="https://github.com/jmonster">
            <img src={authorAvatar.src} width="32" height="32" alt="Johnny Domino" />
            <span>Johnny Domino</span>
          </a>
          <time datetime="2026-07-28T14:00:00-04:00">Jul 28, 2026</time>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="post-prose post-width">
        <h2>What’s it for?</h2>

        <p class="drop-cap">Agents are easy to multiply. Hardware is not. Two builds can target the same Mac; two tests can reset the same phone; two jobs can claim the same GPU. One command can change the resource underneath another, and a green check may belong to the wrong run.</p>

        <p>Workcell gives each resource a first-in, first-out queue. One command owns it; the rest wait in order. When the owner exits, the next starts automatically. Jobs for other resources keep moving.</p>

        <div class="wide-demo" id="workcell">
          <LiveQueue id="workcell-live-queue" />
        </div>

        <h2 id="how-it-works">Install and use</h2>

        <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://workcell-137.pages.dev/install.sh | sh</code></pre>

        <h3>or tell your agent</h3>

        <pre><code>install https://workcell-137.pages.dev/llms.txt</code></pre>

        <p>put Workcell in front of every command that needs <strong>the</strong> resource:</p>

        <pre><code>workcell run macos-xcode --wait -- xcodebuild test</code></pre>

        <ul class="command-options">
          <li><code>macos-xcode</code> is the resource key.<span>Matching keys take turns; different keys run independently.</span></li>
          <li><code>--wait</code> waits in line until the command can run.<span>Omit it to return immediately when the resource is busy.</span></li>
          <li><code>--json</code> returns structured output.<span>Includes the owner, queue position, log path, and a command for waiting.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</MarketingSite>
